[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
Consolidated lessons from prior process experiences: (1) Before moving toward any target object, verify that the intended path is clear; do not assume forward movement will succeed. Obstacles such as stools can block movement, so plan a route around them or adjust the movement plan. (2) A movement obstruction does not necessarily mean the target object is out of reach. Check the object's actual proximity to the robot before predicting pickup failure. (3) Before attempting a Pick action, always verify that the robot's hand is empty. If another object is held, first place or drop it; otherwise the Pick action may fail with an InvalidOperationException. (4) Use failed actions as feedback: if a Move fails due to an obstacle, replan a clear route; if a Pick fails, check hand occupancy and actual reachability before retrying.

## Preliminary Thinking
For putting away the Cup, Bowl, Pot, and Mug: first inspect the scene to locate each object and the intended storage or placement locations. Ensure the robot's hand is empty; if holding anything, place or drop it first. For each item, plan a clear path that avoids obstacles rather than assuming direct forward movement will work. Move near the object, confirm it is within reach and the hand is empty, then attempt Pick. If Move fails due to a blocking obstacle, replan around it. If Pick fails, verify hand occupancy and actual proximity rather than assuming the object is unreachable because of a movement obstruction. After successfully picking an item, navigate to its destination using a clear, obstacle-aware route and Place it. Repeat for the Cup, Bowl, Pot, and Mug, handling one object at a time and adjusting the plan based on action failures.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]